  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water, sanitation and hygiene partnerships to support displaced populations from Zamzam and Al Fasher under the Darfur cholera responseWater, sanitation and hygiene partnerships to support displaced populations from Zamzam and Al Fasher under the Darfur cholera response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ongoing armed clashes in North Darfur have displaced nearly half a million people from Zamzam Camp, most of whom are now in Tawila, where overstretched water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) systems have fuelled a worsening cholera outbreak. Sudan faces a widespread outbreak across 13 states, with over 80,000 cases and 2,000 deaths. Tawila and Al Fasher are among the worst affected. In response, IOM through local partnerships is implementing WASH interventions, including water quality monitoring, water trucking, source rehabilitation, latrine construction, waste management, hygiene promotion, and distribution of hygiene and dignity kits to mitigate the risks of infection and save lives.</narrative>
  </description>
